A type with a bounded number of inhabitants (like bool with 2 or enum with fixed variants), often enabling exhaustive enumeration or decidable equality.

A **type** with a bounded number of inhabitants (like `bool` with 2 or `enum` with fixed variants), often enabling exhaustive enumeration or decidable equality. Contrast with ${fref("programming-language-theory/concepts/infinite-type.td")}.
